  ('cs_philadelphia_geography', 'plc_philadelphia', 'overview', 'Geography',
   '21st century Philadelphia eventually began experiencing a growth in its population in 2007, which continued with incremental annual increases through the present. [1] [2] A migration pattern has been established from New York City to Philadelphia by residents opting for a large city with relative proximity and a lower cost of living . [3] [4] ^ body:not( ):not( ) Purcell, Dylan; Simmons, Karie (March 14, 2013). "Census: Phila. keeps on growing" . philly . Archived from the original on March 19, 2013. ^ "QuickFacts Philadelphia County, Pennsylvania" . United States Census Bureau . Archived from the original on January 1, 2019 . Retrieved April 18, 2019 . ^ Mulligan, Ryan (September 8, 2022). "New Yorkers keep moving to Philadelphia, and local Realtors say the influx has ''raised the bar'' " . bizjournals . Archived from the original on March 5, 2023 . Retrieved February 22, 2023 . ^ Katz, Matt (July 20, 2018). "Leaving New York to Find the American Dream in Philadelphia" . The New York Times . Archived from the original on March 5, 2023 . Retrieved February 22, 2023 .', '["clm_wiki_philadelphia_geography"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
