  ('cs_san-antonio_demographics', 'plc_san-antonio', 'overview', 'Demographics',
   'Neighborhoods Further information: Neighborhoods and districts of San Antonio and Downtown San Antonio Downtown Downtown San Antonio, the city and metro area''s urban core, encompasses many of the city''s famous structures, attractions, and businesses. The central business district is generally understood to cover the northern half of the "Downtown Loop"—the area bordered by Cesar Chavez to the south. Due to the size of the city and its horizontal development, downtown accounts for less than one half of one percent of San Antonio''s geographic area. [1] The Strip (north of Downtown) houses a concentration of clubs and bars catering to the LGBT community. [2] North Central North Central is home to several enclaves and upscale neighborhoods including Castle Hills , Shavano Park, Hollywood Park , Elm Creek, Inwood , Stone Oak , and Rogers Ranch. The area is also the location of upper-middle-class neighborhoods (Deerfield, Churchill Estates, Hunter''s Creek, Oak Meadow, and Summerfield). Northwest Side Northwest Side is the location of the main campus of the University of Texas at San Antonio , the University of Texas Health Science Center at San Antonio , and the Northwest Campus of the University of the Incarnate Word , which includes the Rosenberg School of Optometry. The Medical Center District is also located in Northwest Side. Companies with headquarters in the area include Valero and NuStar Energy . South Side The South Side area of San Antonio is characterized by its predominantly Hispanic neighborhoods, who on average, account for about 65 percent of the population. [3] [4] Large growth came to the South Side when Toyota constructed a manufacturing plant . Palo Alto College and Texas A&amp;M University–San Antonio are also located in the area. East Side Further information: History of African Americans in San Antonio The East Side of San Antonio is home to the San Antonio Stock Show &amp; Rodeo , the Frost Bank Center , and the Freeman Coliseum . This area has the ', '["clm_wiki_san-antonio_demographics"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'place_sections_v2', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
