  ('cs_seattle_history', 'plc_seattle', 'overview', 'History',
   'City in Washington, United States This article is about the city. For other uses, see Seattle (disambiguation) . City in Washington, United States Seattle dᶻidᶻəlal̕ič ( Lushootseed ) City Downtown Seattle skyline with Mount Rainier in the background Space Needle and Climate Pledge Arena , with the Olympic Mountains in the background Seattle Great Wheel Pike Place Market Amazon Spheres Flag Seal Wordmark Nicknames: The Emerald City, Jet City, Rain City Mottoes: The City of Flowers, The City of Goodwill Interactive map of Seattle Seattle Location within Washington (state) Show map of Washington (state) Seattle Location within the United States Show map of the United States Coordinates: 47°36′14″N 122°19′48″W &#xfeff; / &#xfeff; 47.60389°N 122.33000°W &#xfeff; / 47.60389; -122.33000 Country United States State Washington County King Founded November 13, 1851 ( 1851-11-13 ) &#91; a &#93; Incorporated (town status) January 14, 1865 ( 1865-01-14 ) Incorporated (city status) December 2, 1869 ( 1869-12-02 ) Named after Chief Seattle Government • Type Mayor–council • Body Seattle City Council • Mayor Katie Wilson Area [1] • City 142.07 sq mi (367.97 km 2 ) • Land 83.99 sq mi (217.54 km 2 ) • Water 58.08 sq mi (150.43 km 2 ) • Metro 8,186 sq mi (21,202 km 2 ) Elevation [9] 148 ft (45 m) Population ( 2020 ) [2] • City 737,015 • Estimate (2025) [3] 784,777 • Rank 54th in North America 18th in the United States 1st in Washington • Density 9,302.2/sq mi (3,591.59/km 2 ) • Urban [5] 3,544,011 (US: 13th ) • Urban density 3,607/sq mi (1,392.7/km 2 ) • Metro [4] 4,018,762 (US: 15th ) Demonym Seattleite [6] or Seattlite [7] GDP [8] • Metro $604.065 billion (2024) Time zone UTC−8 ( PST ) • Summer ( DST ) UTC−7 ( PDT ) ZIP Codes ZIP Codes [10] [11] 98101–98119, 98121–98122, 98124–98127, 98129, 98131, 98133–98134, 98136, 98138–98139, 98141, 98144–98146, 98148, 98154–98155, 98158, 98160–98161, 98164–98166, 98168, 98170, 98174–98175, 98177–98178, 98181, 98185, 98188, 98190–98191, 98194–98195, 98198–98199 Area code 206 , 564 FIPS code 53-63000 GNIS feature ID 2411856 [9] Website seattle Symbols Motto The City of Flowers; the City of Goodwill [12] Song "Seattle the Peerless City" [12] Bird Great blue heron [12] Flower Dahlia [12] Preview warning: Page using Template:Infobox settlement with deprecated parameter blank1_info . Replace with custom_data1_sec1 . Preview warning: Page using Template:Infobox settlement with deprecated parameter blank_info . Replace with custom_data_sec1 .', '["clm_wiki_seattle_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'place_sections_v2', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
