  ('cs_washington-dc_history', 'plc_washington-dc', 'overview', 'History',
   'Federal capital district of the United States Not to be confused with Washington (state) . Several terms redirect here. For other uses, see District of Columbia (disambiguation) ,&#32; United States capital (disambiguation) &#44;&#32;and&#32; D.C. (disambiguation) . Place in the United States Washington, D.C. Federal capital city and federal district District of Columbia From top, left to right : The U.S. Capitol , the Washington Monument and Lincoln Memorial on the National Mall , Washington National Cathedral , The Wharf , storefronts in Adams Morgan , Air and Space Museum , White House Flag Seal Nicknames: D.C., The District Motto: Justitia Omnibus (English: Justice for All ) Anthem: "Washington" [1] Neighborhoods of Washington, D.C. Interactive map of Washington, D.C. Washington, D.C. Location within the United States Show map of the United States Washington, D.C. Location within North America Show map of North America Coordinates: 38°54′17″N 77°00′59″W &#xfeff; / &#xfeff; 38.90472°N 77.01639°W &#xfeff; / 38.90472; -77.01639 &#xfeff; ( District of Columbia ) Country United States Residence Act July 16, 1790 Organized February 27, 1801 Consolidated February 21, 1871 Home Rule Act December 24, 1973 Named after George Washington Columbia Government • Type Mayor–council • Mayor Muriel Bowser ( D ) • D.C. Council List Phil Mendelson (D), Chair Anita Bonds (D), At‑large Christina Henderson ( I ), At‑large Robert White (D), At‑large Kenyan McDuffie (I), At‑large Brianne Nadeau (D), Ward 1 Brooke Pinto (D), Ward 2 Matthew Frumin (D), Ward 3 Janeese Lewis George (D), Ward 4 Zachary Parker (D), Ward 5 Charles Allen (D), Ward 6 Wendell Felder (D), Ward 7 • U.S. House Eleanor Holmes Norton (D), Delegate (At-large) Area • Federal capital city and federal district 68.35 sq mi (177.0 km 2 ) • Land 61.126 sq mi (158.32 km 2 ) • Water 7.224 sq mi (18.71 km 2 ) Highest elevation &#32;( Fort Reno Park ) 409 ft (125 m) Lowest elevation &#32;( Potomac River ) 0 ft (0 m) Population ( 2020 ) [3] • Federal capital city and federal district 689,545 • Estimate (2025) [4] 693,645 • Rank 67th in North America 22nd in the United States • Density 11,280.4/sq mi (4,355.39/km 2 ) • Urban [5] 5,174,759 (US: 8th ) • Urban density 3,997/sq mi (1,543.4/km 2 ) • Metro [2] 6,304,975 (US: 7th ) Demonym Washingtonian [6] GDP [7] • Federal capital city and district $184.298 billion (2024) • Metro $749.108 billion (2024) Time zone UTC−05:00 ( EST ) • Summer ( DST ) UTC−04:00 ( EDT ) ZIP Codes ', '["clm_wiki_washington-dc_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
