   'This article is about the city. For the song, see Memphis, Tennessee (song) . "Memphis, United States" redirects here. For other places, see Memphis . City in Tennessee, United States Memphis City Downtown Memphis skyline Beale Street FedExForum Graceland Memphis Pyramid Flag Seal Wordmark Nicknames: Bluff City, Home of the Blues, Grind City, The 901 Interactive map of Memphis Memphis Location in Tennessee Show map of Tennessee Memphis Location in the United States Show map of the United States Coordinates: 35°8′46″N 90°3′7″W &#xfeff; / &#xfeff; 35.14611°N 90.05194°W &#xfeff; / 35.14611; -90.05194 Country United States State Tennessee County Shelby Founded May 22, 1819 ( 1819-05-22 ) Incorporated December 19, 1826 ( 1826-12-19 ) Dissolved January 31, 1879 ( 1879-01-31 ) [1] Rechartered April 5, 1893 ( 1893-04-05 ) [2] Founded by John Overton , James Winchester , and Andrew Jackson Named after Memphis, Egypt Government • Mayor Paul Young ( D ) Area [8] • City 302.57 sq mi (783.66 km 2 ) • Land 294.92 sq mi (763.83 km 2 ) • Water 7.63 sq mi (19.77 km 2 ) Elevation 338 ft (103 m) Population ( 2020 ) [3] • City 633,104 • Estimate (2024) [9] 610,919 • Rank 77th in North America 28th in the United States 2nd in Tennessee • Density 2,146.7/sq mi (828.85/km 2 ) • Urban 1,056,190 ( US: 45th ) • Urban density 2,150/sq mi (830.1/km 2 ) • Metro [4] 1,345,425 ( US: 45th ) Demonym Memphian GDP [5] • Metro $102.934 billion (2023) Time zone UTC−6 ( CST ) • Summer ( DST ) UTC−5 ( CDT ) ZIP Codes ZIP Codes [6] 37501, 37544, 38101, 38103–38109, 38111–38120, 38122, 38124–38128, 38130–38139, 38141, 38145, 38148, 38150–38152, 38157, 38159, 38161, 38163, 38166–38168, 38173–38175, 38177, 38181–38182, 38184, 38186–38188, 38190, 38193–38194, 38197 Area code 901 FIPS code 47-48000 [7] Website memphistn Preview warning: Page using Template:Infobox settlement with deprecated parameter settlement_type . Replace with type . Preview warning: Page using Template:Infobox settlement with deprecat