VALUES
  ('cs_orlando_history', 'plc_orlando', 'overview', 'History',
   'Orlando ( As You Like It ) Lake Lucerne, c. 1905 The final variation has the city named after the protagonist in the Shakespeare play As You Like It . [1] In 1975, Judge Donald A. Cheney put forth a new version of the story in an Orlando Sentinel article. [2] Cheney (a local historian and then chairman of the county historical commission [3] ) recounted a story told to him by his father, Judge John Moses Cheney (a major figure in Orlando''s history, who arrived in Orlando in 1885). The elder Cheney recounted that another gentleman at that time, James Speer, proposed the name Orlando after the character in As You Like It . [1] According to Cheney, Speer, "was a gentleman of culture and an admirer of William Shakespeare ..." [2] Quoting a letter that Speer wrote, "Orlando was a veritable Forest of Arden , the locale of As You Like It ." [4] Speer''s descendants have also confirmed this version of the naming and the legend has continued to grow. [2] This account also has some validity in that, as mentioned above, Speer was instrumental in changing the name of the settlement from Jernigan to Orlando, though he may have used the Orlando Reeves legend in lieu of his true intent to use the Shakespearean character. According to yet another version of the story, Orlando may have been the name of one of his employees. [1] [5] One of downtown Orlando ''s major streets is named Rosalind Avenue; Rosalind is the heroine of As You Like It , but this could also be a coincidence. ^ a b c Cite error: The named reference Andrews1998 was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ a b c Cite error: The named reference Dickinson, Cheney was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ body:not( ):not( ) "About" . Historical Society of Central Florida . Retrieved April 17, 2022 . ^ Reflections . Fall 2015 Vol. 13 No. 4. Retrieved&#32;March 1, 2017 . ^ Cite error: The named reference travel was invoked but never defined (see the help page ).', '["clm_wiki_orlando_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'place_sections_v2', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   20, 1, 1, unixepoch());
