   version, created_at, updated_at, display_order, claim_count, source_count, last_verified_at)
VALUES
  ('cs_pittsburgh_geography', 'plc_pittsburgh', 'overview', 'Geography',
   '21st century During the late 2000s recession , Pittsburgh was economically strong, adding jobs when most cities were losing them. It was one of the few cities in the United States to see housing property values rise. Between 2006 and 2011, the Pittsburgh metropolitan statistical area (MSA) experienced over 10% appreciation in housing prices, the highest appreciation of the largest 25 metropolitan statistical areas in the United States, with 22 of the largest 25 metropolitan statistical areas experiencing depreciations in housing values. [1] In September 2009, the 2009 G20 Pittsburgh summit was held in Pittsburgh. [2] In April 2026, Pittsburgh hosted the NFL draft for the first time. [3] The event hosted over 805,000 people in the city during the 3 day event. [4] ^ body:not( ):not( ) Briem, Christopher (December 30, 2011). "More Pittsburgh real estate trends" . Nullspace . Retrieved January 1, 2012 . ^ "US to host next G20 world meeting" . BBC News . May 28, 2009 . Retrieved May 22, 2010 . ^ "Why Pittsburgh is a natural fit to host the 2026 NFL draft : NPR" . www . Retrieved July 17, 2026 . ^ "2026 NFL Draft in Pittsburgh | Pittsburgh Steelers - Steelers " . www . Retrieved July 17, 2026 .', '["clm_wiki_pittsburgh_geography"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'place_sections_v2', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   30, 1, 1, unixepoch());
