  ('cs_milwaukee_history', 'plc_milwaukee', 'overview', 'History',
   'Largest city in Wisconsin, United States This article is about the city in Wisconsin. For the former town in Wisconsin, see Milwaukee (town), Wisconsin . For other uses, see Milwaukee (disambiguation) . City in Wisconsin, United States Milwaukee City Downtown Milwaukee Milwaukee City Hall Milwaukee Riverwalk Harley Museum Milwaukee Art Museum American Family Field Mitchell Park Horticultural Conservatory Flag Seal Logo Nicknames: Cream City, Brew City, MKE, City of Festivals, The Mil, The 414 [1] [2] [3] Interactive map of Milwaukee Milwaukee Location within Wisconsin Show map of Wisconsin Milwaukee Location within the United States Show map of the United States Coordinates: 43°03′N 87°57′W &#xfeff; / &#xfeff; 43.05°N 87.95°W &#xfeff; / 43.05; -87.95 Country United States State Wisconsin Counties Milwaukee , Washington , Waukesha Incorporated January 31, 1846 &#59;&#32;180 years ago ( 1846-01-31 ) Founded by Solomon Juneau , Byron Kilbourn , and George H. Walker Named after Potawatomi for "gathering place by the water" Government • Type Strong mayor-council • Body Milwaukee Common Council • Mayor Cavalier Johnson ( D ) Area [4] • City 96.82 sq mi (250.75 km 2 ) • Land 96.19 sq mi (249.12 km 2 ) • Water 0.63 sq mi (1.63 km 2 ) Elevation 617 ft (188 m) Population ( 2020 ) [5] • City 577,222 • Estimate (2025) [6] 562,407 • Rank 85th in North America 31st in the United States 1st in Wisconsin • Density 6,001.1/sq mi (2,317.0/km 2 ) • Urban 1,306,795 ( US: 38th ) • Urban density 2,818/sq mi (1,088.2/km 2 ) • Metro [7] 1,574,731 ( US: 40th ) • CSA 2,049,805 ( US: 33rd ) Demonym Milwaukeean GDP [8] • Metro $130.857 billion (2022) • Per capita $83,098 (2022) Time zone UTC−6 ( CST ) • Summer ( DST ) UTC−5 ( CDT ) ZIP Codes 53172, 532XX 53172, 53201–53216, 53218–53228, 53233–53234, 53237, 53259, 53263, 53267–53268, 53274, 53278, 53288, 53290, 53293, 53295 Area code 414 FIPS code 55-53000 [9] GNIS feature ID 1577901 [10] Website city Preview warning: Page using Template:In