VALUES
  ('cs_wichita_demographics', 'plc_wichita', 'overview', 'Demographics',
   '19th century Darius Sales Munger House, built in 1868, is the oldest surviving building in Wichita (at Old Cowtown Museum ). [1] Claimed first by France as part of Louisiana and later acquired by the United States with the Louisiana Purchase in 1803, it became part of Kansas Territory in 1854 and then the state of Kansas in 1861. [2] [3] The Wichita people returned in 1863, driven from their land in Indian Territory by Confederate forces in the American Civil War , and established a settlement on the banks of the Little Arkansas. [4] [5] [6] During this period, trader Jesse Chisholm established a trading post at the site, one of several along a trail extending south to Texas which became known as the Chisholm Trail . [7] In 1867, after the war, the Wichita returned to Indian Territory. [4] In 1868, trader James R. Mead was among a group of investors who established a town company, and surveyor Darius Munger built a log structure for the company to serve as a hotel, community center, and post office. [8] [9] Business opportunities attracted area hunters and traders, and a new settlement began to form. That summer, Mead and others organized the Wichita Town Company, naming the settlement after the Wichita tribe. [5] In 1870, Munger and German immigrant William "Dutch Bill" Greiffenstein filed plats laying out the city''s first streets. [9] Wichita formally incorporated as a city on July 21, 1870. [8] A 1915 railroad map of Sedgwick County, showing many railroads that previously passed through Wichita Wichita''s position on the Chisholm Trail made it a destination for cattle drives traveling north from Texas to access railroads, which led to markets in eastern U.S. cities. [7] [10] The Atchison, Topeka and Santa Fe Railway reached the city in 1872. [11] As a result, Wichita became a railhead for the cattle drives, earning it the nickname "Cowtown". [7] [10] Across the Arkansas River, the town of Delano became an entertainment destination for cattlemen thanks to its saloo', '["clm_wiki_wichita_demographics"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'place_sections_v2', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
