  ('cs_st-louis_history', 'plc_st-louis', 'overview', 'History',
   'Independent city in Missouri, United States This article is about the city in Missouri, United States. For other uses, see St. Louis (disambiguation) . "St. Louis City" redirects here. For the Major League Soccer Team, see St. Louis City SC . html body This article needs more citations . Please help improve this article by adding citations to reliable sources . Unsourced material may be challenged and removed . Find sources: "St. Louis" – news · newspapers · books · scholar · JSTOR ( July 2024 ) ( Learn how and when to remove this message ) Independent city in Missouri, United States St. Louis Independent city The Old Courthouse and Gateway Arch in Downtown St. Louis Saint Louis Art Museum Busch Stadium Missouri Botanical Garden Union Station Flag Seal Nicknames: "Gateway to the West", [1] The Gateway City, [1] Mound City, [2] The Lou, [3] Rome of the West, [4] River City, The STL, St. Lou Interactive map of St. Louis St. Louis Location within Missouri Show map of Missouri St. Louis Location within the United States Show map of the United States Coordinates: 38°37′38″N 90°11′52″W &#xfeff; / &#xfeff; 38.62722°N 90.19778°W &#xfeff; / 38.62722; -90.19778 Country United States State Missouri CSA St. Louis–St. Charles–Farmington, MO–IL Metro St. Louis, MO-IL Founded February 14, 1764 Incorporated 1822 Named after Louis IX of France Government • Type Mayor–council • Body Board of Aldermen • Mayor Cara Spencer ( D ) • President, Board of Aldermen Megan Green (D) • Treasurer Adam Layne • Comptroller Donna Baringer (D) • Congressional representative Wesley Bell (D) Area [5] • Independent city 66.17 sq mi (171.39 km 2 ) • Land 61.72 sq mi (159.85 km 2 ) • Water 4.45 sq mi (11.53 km 2 ) • Urban 910.4 sq mi (2,357.8 km 2 ) • Metro 8,458 sq mi (21,910 km 2 ) Elevation [6] 466 ft (142 m) Highest elevation [7] 614 ft (187 m) Population ( 2020 ) [9] • Independent city 301,578 • Estimate (2025) [8] 278,144 • Rank US: 82nd Midwest: 13th Missouri: 2nd • Density 4,886.2/sq mi (1,88