VALUES
  ('cs_hollywood-sign_demographics', 'plc_hollywood-sign', 'overview', 'Demographics',
   'Deterioration and restoration In the 1970s, the sign reached its most dilapidated state. This image was taken shortly before the sign''s 1978 restoration. 1940s In time, the sign deteriorated. The letter H was destroyed in early 1944. A United Press report in 1949 indicated that winds were to blame, [1] while the Los Angeles Times said that the H was destroyed by "vandals or windstorms." [2] In 1949, the sign drew complaints from local residents, who called it an "eyesore and detriment to the community" and advocated its demolition. The Hollywood Chamber of Commerce protested against the sign''s removal and offered to repair it. [2] The Chamber entered into a contract with the City of Los Angeles Parks Department to repair and rebuild the sign. The contract stipulated that "LAND" be removed to spell "Hollywood" and reflect the district, not the "Hollywoodland" housing development. [3] The restoration and removal of the "land" portion of the sign was conducted in September 1949. [1] 1970s Once all wood, the sign was rebuilt in metal letters supported by a structural steel framework. The sign''s unprotected wood-and-sheet-metal structure deteriorated over the years. After a severe windstorm on February 10, 1978, the first O was splintered and broken, resembling a lowercase u , and the third O had fallen down completely, leaving the now-dilapidated sign reading "HuLLYWO D." [4] [5] In 1978, the Chamber set out to replace the severely deteriorated sign with a more permanent structure. Nine donors gave US$27,778 each (totaling US$250,000, equivalent to $1,230,000&#32;in 2025) to sponsor replacement letters, made of steel supported by steel columns on a concrete foundation (see § Donors , below) . [6] The new letters were 44 ft (13.4 m) tall and ranged from 31 to 39 ft (9.4 to 11.9 m) wide. The new version of the sign was unveiled on November 11, 1978, as the culmination of a live CBS television special commemorating the 75th anniversary of Hollywood''s incorporation as a cit', '["clm_wiki_hollywood-sign_demographics"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'place_sections_v2', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
-- 58. Golden Gate Park (slug=golden-gate-park, wiki='Golden Gate Park', type=landmark)
