VALUES
  ('cs_madison-square-garden_history', 'plc_madison-square-garden', 'overview', 'History',
   'Multi-purpose indoor arena in New York City, U.S. This article is about the current New York City arena, open since 1968. For other uses, see MSG (disambiguation) . Madison Square Garden MSG The Garden The World''s Most Famous Arena The Mecca Madison Square Garden in 2019 Madison Square Garden Location in Manhattan Show map of Manhattan Madison Square Garden Location in New York City Show map of New York City Madison Square Garden Location in New York State Show map of New York Madison Square Garden Location in the United States Show map of the United States Address 4 Pennsylvania Plaza Location Midtown Manhattan , New York City, U.S. Coordinates 40°45′2″N 73°59′37″W &#xfeff; / &#xfeff; 40.75056°N 73.99361°W &#xfeff; / 40.75056; -73.99361 Owner Madison Square Garden Entertainment Capacity Basketball : 19,812 [1] Boxing / MMA : 20,789 Concert : 22,000 Ice hockey : 18,006 [1] Pro wrestling : 18,538 [2] Field size 820,000 sq ft (76,000 m 2 ) Public transit Amtrak : Penn Station LIRR : Penn Station NJ Transit : Penn Station New York City Subway : &#8203; &#8203; 34th Street–Penn Station (7th Ave) &#8203; &#8203; 34th Street–Penn Station (8th Ave) &#8203; &#8203; &#8203; &#8203; &#8203; &#8203; &#8203; 34th Street–Herald Square PATH : 33rd Street New York City Bus : M4 , M7 , M20 , M34 SBS , M34A SBS , Q32 , BxM2 at 34th Street–Penn Station Construction Groundbreaking October 29, 1964 [3] Opened 1879 , 1890 , 1925 (former locations) February 11, 1968 &#59;&#32;58 years ago ( 1968-02-11 ) (current location) Renovated 1989–1991 2011–2013 Cost $123 million ($1.14 billion in 2025 dollars [4] ) Renovation (1991): $200 million ($473 million in 2025 dollars [4] ) Renovation (2011–2013): $1 billion ($1.38 billion in 2025 dollars [4] ) Architect Charles Luckman Associates Brisbin Brook Beynon Architects Structural engineer Severud Associates [5] Services engineer Syska &amp; Hennessy, Inc. [6] General contractor Turner / Del E. Webb [6] Tenants New York Rangers ( NHL ) (1968–present) New York Knicks ( NBA ) (1968–present) St. John''s Red Storm ( NCAA ) (1969–present) New York Raiders/Golden Blades ( WHA ) (1972–1973) New York Apples ( WTT ) (1977–1978) New York Stars ( WBL ) (1979–1980) New York Cosmos ( NASL ) (1983–1984) New York Knights ( AFL ) (1988) New York CityHawks ( AFL ) (1997–1998) New York Liberty ( WNBA ) (1997–2010, 2014–2017) New York Titans ( NLL ) (2007–2009) Website msg /madison-square-garden Madison Square Garden , colloquially known as the Garden or by', '["clm_wiki_madison-square-garden_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
