  ('cs_pentagon_geography', 'plc_pentagon', 'overview', 'Geography',
   'Derivation of the area formula The area of any regular polygon is: A = 1 2 P r {\displaystyle A={\frac {1}{2}}Pr} where P is the perimeter of the polygon, and r is the inradius (equivalently the apothem ). Substituting the regular pentagon''s values for P and r gives the formula A = 1 2 &#x22C5; 5 t &#x22C5; t tan &#x2061; ( 3 &#x03C0; 10 ) 2 = 5 t 2 tan &#x2061; ( 3 &#x03C0; 10 ) 4 {\displaystyle A={\frac {1}{2}}\cdot 5t\cdot {\frac {t\tan {\mathord {\left({\frac {3\pi }{10}}\right)}}}{2}}={\frac {5t^{2}\tan {\mathord {\left({\frac {3\pi }{10}}\right)}}}{4}}} with side length t .', '["clm_wiki_pentagon_geography"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
