  ('cs_pentagon_demographics', 'plc_pentagon', 'overview', 'Demographics',
   'Inradius Similar to every regular convex polygon, the regular convex pentagon has an inscribed circle . The apothem , which is the radius r of the inscribed circle, of a regular pentagon is related to the side length t by r = t 2 tan &#x2061; ( &#x03C0; 5 ) = t 2 5 &#x2212; 20 &#x2248; 0.6882 &#x22C5; t . {\displaystyle r={\frac {t}{2\tan {\mathord {\left({\frac {\pi }{5}}\right)}}}}={\frac {t}{2{\sqrt {5-{\sqrt {20}}}}}}\approx 0.6882\cdot t.}', '["clm_wiki_pentagon_demographics"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
