  ('cs_smithsonian-institution_demographics', 'plc_smithsonian-institution', 'overview', 'Demographics',
   'Research centers The Smithsonian has eight research centers, located in Washington, D.C.; Front Royal, Virginia ; Edgewater, Maryland ; Suitland, Maryland ; Fort Pierce, Florida ; Cambridge, Massachusetts ; and Panama . [1] [2] [3] [4] [5] [6] [7] Formerly two separate entities, the Smithsonian Libraries and Smithsonian Archives merged into a single research center in 2020. [8] Research center [1] Area of focus Location [7] [3] [2] [5] Opened Ref. Archives of American Art History of the visual arts in the United States Washington, D.C. New York City 1954 1970 &#91; note 1 &#93; [9] Smithsonian Astrophysical Observatory Astrophysics Cambridge, Massachusetts 1890 [6] Museum Conservation Institute Conservation Suitland, Maryland 1965 [4] Smithsonian Conservation Biology Institute (affiliated with the National Zoo ) Veterinary medicine , reproductive physiology and conservation biology Front Royal, Virginia 1974 [5] Smithsonian Environmental Research Center Coastal ecosystems Edgewater, Maryland 1965 [3] Smithsonian Libraries and Archives Science, art, history and culture, and museology information and reference Washington, D.C. 1968 &#91; note 2 &#93; 2020 &#91; note 3 &#93; [8] Smithsonian Marine Station at Fort Pierce (affiliated with the National Museum of Natural History ) Floridian marine ecosystems and lifeforms Fort Pierce, Florida 1981 1999 &#91; note 4 &#93; [10] Smithsonian Tropical Research Institute Tropical ecology and its interactions with human welfare Panama 1923 &#91; note 5 &#93; 1946 &#91; note 6 &#93; 1966 &#91; note 7 &#93; [7] ^ a b Cite error: The named reference Fact was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ a b body:not( ):not( ) "Smithsonian Marine Station at Fort Pierce" . Smithsonian Institution . Archived from the original on November 30, 2022 . Retrieved December 24, 2022 . ^ a b c "Smithsonian Environmental Research Center" . Smithsonian Environmental Research Center . Smithsonian Institution . Retrieved December 24, 2022 . ^ ', '["clm_wiki_smithsonian-institution_demographics"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'place_sections_v2', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
