VALUES
  ('cs_pro-football-hall-of-fame_history', 'plc_pro-football-hall-of-fame', 'overview', 'History',
   'Professional sports hall of fame in Canton, Ohio, U.S. Pro Football Hall of Fame Canton Location in the United States Show map of the United States Canton Location in Ohio Show map of Ohio Established September 7, 1963 &#59;&#32;62 years ago ( 1963-09-07 ) Location 2121 George Halas Dr. NW, Canton, Ohio , U.S. Coordinates 40°49′16″N 81°23′52″W &#xfeff; / &#xfeff; 40.82111°N 81.39778°W &#xfeff; / 40.82111; -81.39778 Type Professional sports hall of fame President Jim Porter Website profootballhof The Pro Football Hall of Fame is the hall of fame for professional American football , located in Canton, Ohio . Opened on September 7, 1963, [1] the Hall of Fame enshrines exceptional figures in the sport of professional football, including players, coaches, officials, franchise owners, and front-office personnel, almost all of whom made their primary contributions to the game in the National Football League (NFL). However, the Hall of Fame has no official affiliation with the NFL. [2] [3] As of 2026 &#91;update&#93; , there are a total of 387 members of the Hall of Fame. [4] Between four and nine new inductees are normally enshrined every year. For the 2020 class, a 20-person group consisting of five modern-era players and an additional 15 members, known as the "Centennial Slate", were elected to the Hall of Fame to celebrate the 100th anniversary of the NFL. [5] The Chicago Bears have the most inductees, with 32 (41, including players with minor portion of their career with team). Canton is often used as shorthand or metonym for the Hall of Fame. ^ body:not( ):not( ) Maroon, Tarin; Maroon, Margaret; Holbert, Craig (2006). Akron-Canton Football Heritage . Arcadia Publishing. ISBN 9780738540788 . Retrieved January 5, 2022 . ^ Rumsey, David (August 2, 2023). "Pro Football Hall of Fame''s Complicated Canton Relationship" . frontofficesports . Retrieved January 28, 2026 . ^ Volin, Ben (February 2, 2026). "Commissioner Roger Goodell: Hall vote out of the league''s hands" . The Boston Globe . Retrieved February 3, 2026 . It''s the Pro Football Hall of Fame, it''s not the NFL Hall of Fame, and it is completely and entirely out of the hands of the league. ^ "Pro Football Hall of Fame Enshrinees" . Retrieved February 11, 2023 . ^ "15-person centennial slate for HOF revealed Jan. 15 on NFLN" . NFL. January 8, 2020.', '["clm_wiki_pro-football-hall-of-fame_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'place_sections_v2', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
