  ('cs_dartmouth-college_history', 'plc_dartmouth-college', 'overview', 'History',
   'Private university in Hanover, New Hampshire, US This article is about the private university in Hanover, New Hampshire. For the public university in Massachusetts, see University of Massachusetts Dartmouth . For the military college in Dartmouth, United Kingdom, see Britannia Royal Naval College Dartmouth . For other uses, see Dartmouth (disambiguation) . Dartmouth College Latin : Collegii Dartmuthensis [1] Motto Vox clamantis in deserto ( Latin – A quotation from the Book of Isaiah in the Old Testament ) Motto in English "A voice crying out in the wilderness" [2] Type Private research university Established December 13, 1769 &#59;&#32;256 years ago ( 1769-12-13 ) [3] Accreditation NECHE Academic affiliations AAU COFHE NAICU UArctic Space-grant Endowment $9 billion (2025) [4] Budget $1.5 billion (2024) [5] President Sian Beilock Provost Santiago Schnell Academic staff 943 (fall 2018) [2] Administrative staff 2,938 full time, 328 part time (Fall 2018) [6] Students 6,746 (fall 2023) [7] Undergraduates 4,447 (fall 2023) [7] Postgraduates 2,299 (fall 2023) [7] Location Hanover, New Hampshire , United States 43°42′12″N 72°17′18″W &#xfeff; / &#xfeff; 43.70333°N 72.28833°W &#xfeff; / 43.70333; -72.28833 Campus 31,869 acres (128.97 km 2 ) (total) Remote town [8] Newspaper The Dartmouth Colors Dartmouth green and white [9] Nickname Big Green Sporting affiliations NCAA Division I FCS – Ivy League ECAC Hockey NEISA IRA EISA EARC EAWRC Website home Dear Old Dartmouth The Dartmouth Decibelles in 2021 file help Dartmouth College ( / ˈ d ɑːr t m ə θ / DART -məth ) is a private Ivy League research university in Hanover, New Hampshire , United States. Established in 1769 by Eleazar Wheelock to train Native American Christian missionaries, Dartmouth is one of the nine colonial colleges chartered before the American Revolution . Following a liberal arts curriculum, Dartmouth provides undergraduate instruction in 40 academic departments and interdisciplinary programs, including 60 majors in the humanities, social sciences, natural sciences, and engineering. [10] In addition to the undergraduate faculty of arts and sciences, Dartmouth has four professional and graduate schools: the Geisel School of Medicine , the Thayer School of Engineering , the Tuck School of Business , and the Guarini School of Graduate and Advanced Studies. [11] The university also has affiliations with the Dartmouth–Hitchcock Medical Center . Dartmouth is home to the Rockefeller Center for Public Policy', '["clm_wiki_dartmouth-college_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'place_sections_v2', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   20, 1, 1, unixepoch());
