  ('cs_dartmouth-college_demographics', 'plc_dartmouth-college', 'overview', 'Demographics',
   'Research Dartmouth College is a research institution designated by the Carnegie Classification of Institutions of Higher Education as having "very high research activity". [1] In 2019, Dartmouth College was elected to the Association of American Universities (AAU), an organization of 69 research universities. [2] Faculty members have been at the forefront of such major academic developments as the Dartmouth Workshop , the Dartmouth Time-Sharing System , Dartmouth BASIC , and Dartmouth ALGOL 30 . In 2005, sponsored project awards to Dartmouth faculty research amounted to $169 million. [3] In 2017, Eric Fossum , a professor of engineering at Dartmouth College, was awarded the Queen Elizabeth Prize for his work on imaging sensor technology. [4] The Pfizer–BioNTech COVID-19 vaccine , which was approved in 2021, was based on findings that originated in a science lab at the college. [5] In 2024, researchers at Dartmouth received a $31.3 million grant from the federal government to further their study of prostate cancer. [6] In 2025, Dartmouth received approximately $97 million worth of funding from the National Institutes of Health . [7] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Dartmouth College" . Carnegie Classification of Institutions of Higher Education® . Retrieved May 5, 2025 . ^ "Three Leading Research Universities Join the Association of American Universities (AAU)" . Aau . November 6, 2019. Archived from the original on April 29, 2020 . Retrieved March 5, 2020 . ^ Cite error: The named reference Academics &amp; Research was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ Cookson, Clive (February 1, 2017). "Digital imaging inventors win engineering''s £1m Queen Elizabeth Prize" . Financial Times . ^ Feingold, Jeff (January 7, 2021). "Groundwork for Covid-19 vaccine laid at Dartmouth" . NHBR . ^ Sauchelli, Liz (August 13, 2024). "Dartmouth Team Gets $31.3 Million for Prostate Cancer Research" . Valley News . ^ Zahneis, Megan (March 3, 2025). " ''Let''s Not Overreact'': How One College''', '["clm_wiki_dartmouth-college_demographics"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'place_sections_v2', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
