  ('cs_northwestern-university_history', 'plc_northwestern-university', 'overview', 'History',
   'University in Evanston, Illinois, US This article is about the private research university in Illinois, United States. For other uses, see Northwestern University (disambiguation) . Northwestern University Motto Quaecumque sunt vera ( Latin ) On seal: Ὁ Λόγος πλήρης χάριτος καὶ ἀληθείας ( Greek ) Motto in English "Whatsoever things are true" ( Philippians 4:8 AV ) "The Word full of grace and truth" ( John 1:14 ) Type Private research university Established January 28, 1851 &#59;&#32;175 years ago ( January 28, 1851 ) Accreditation HLC Academic affiliations AAU COFHE IAMSCU NAICU URA Space-grant Endowment $15.3 billion (2025) [1] Budget $3.3 billion (2024) (excluding the health system) [2] President Mung Chiang Provost Erik Luijten Faculty 4,018 (fall 2021) [3] Students 22,801 (fall 2023) [4] Undergraduates 8,846 (fall 2023) [4] Postgraduates 13,955 (fall 2023) [4] Location Evanston, Illinois , United States 42°03′21″N 87°40′29″W &#xfeff; / &#xfeff; 42.05583°N 87.67472°W &#xfeff; / 42.05583; -87.67472 Campus 240 acres (97 ha) Small city [5] Other campuses Chicago Coral Gables San Francisco Washington, D.C. Doha Newspaper The Daily Northwestern Colors Purple and white [6] Nickname Wildcats Sporting affiliations NCAA Division I FBS – Big Ten CCFC Mascot Willie the Wildcat Website northwestern Northwestern University ( NU ) is a private research university in Evanston, Illinois , United States. Established in 1851, it is the oldest chartered university in Illinois. Northwestern was initially affiliated with the Methodist Episcopal Church but later became non-sectarian . By 1900, the university was the third-largest university in the United States , after Michigan and Harvard . &#91; citation needed &#93; Northwestern became a founding member of the Big Ten Conference in 1896 and joined the Association of American Universities in 1917. Northwestern is composed of eleven undergraduate, graduate, and professional schools in the fields of management , law , journalism , engineering , medicine , and others. As of 2024, the university had an endowment of $15.6 billion, an annual budget of around $3.3 billion, [7] [8] and research funding of over $1 billion. [9] The university fields 19 intercollegiate athletic teams, the Northwestern Wildcats , which compete in the NCAA Division I in the Big Ten Conference . As of September 2020, 37 Nobel Prize laureates and 2 Fields Medalists [10] were affiliated with Northwestern as alumni or faculty . In addition, Northwestern ha', '["clm_wiki_northwestern-university_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
