VALUES
  ('cs_duke-university_demographics', 'plc_duke-university', 'overview', 'Demographics',
   'Expansion and growth Engineering , which had been taught at Duke since 1903, became a separate school in 1939. The university president''s official residence, the J. Deryl Hart House , was completed in 1934. In athletics, Duke hosted and competed in the first Rose Bowl ever played outside California in Wallace Wade Stadium in 1942; the second such game was played in Arlington, Texas , in 2021, moved as a result of the COVID-19 pandemic . [1] [2] During World War II, Duke was one of 131 colleges and universities nationally that took part in the V-12 Navy College Training Program which offered students a path to a navy commission. [3] In 1963 the Board of Trustees officially desegregated the undergraduate college. [4] Duke enrolled its first Black graduate students in 1961. [5] The school did not admit Black undergraduates until September 1963. The teaching staff remained all-white until 1966. [6] Increased activism on campus during the 1960s prompted Martin Luther King Jr. to speak at the university in November 1964 on the progress of the Civil Rights Movement . [7] Following Douglas Knight ''s resignation from the office of university president, Terry Sanford , the former governor of North Carolina, was elected president of the university in 1969, propelling The Fuqua School of Business '' opening, the William R. Perkins library completion, and the founding of the Institute of Policy Sciences and Public Affairs (now the Sanford School of Public Policy). [8] [9] The separate Woman''s College merged back with Trinity as the liberal arts college for both men and women in 1972. Beginning in the 1970s, Duke administrators began a long-term effort to strengthen Duke''s reputation both nationally and internationally. Interdisciplinary work was emphasized, as was recruiting minority faculty and students. During this time it also became the birthplace of the first Physician Assistant degree program in the United States. [10] [11] [12] Duke University Hospital was finished in 1980', '["clm_wiki_duke-university_demographics"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'place_sections_v2', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
-- 104. Vanderbilt University (slug=vanderbilt-university, wiki='Vanderbilt University', type=university)
