VALUES
  ('cs_vanderbilt-university_demographics', 'plc_vanderbilt-university', 'overview', 'Demographics',
   'Connections to slavery Many of the university''s early leaders had prominent ties to slavery and the Confederacy before the Civil War. Frank Vanderbilt was "a Confederate sympathizer" during the Civil War. [1] McTyeire was born into a slave-owning family and authored an essay in favor of slavery. [2] Garland owned "up to 60 slaves" before the Civil War. [2] One of the founding trustees, Hezekiah William Foote , was a Confederate veteran and the owner of four plantations in Mississippi , including Mount Holly . [3] The Treasurer of the Board of Trust from 1872 to 1875, Alexander Little Page Green , whose portrait hangs in Kirkland Hall, [4] was a Methodist preacher and a former slave owner. [5] His son-in-law, Robert A. Young , was a Methodist minister who served as the Financial Secretary on the Board of Trust from 1874 to 1882, retiring from the board in 1902. [6] The Elliston family, who owned slaves, donated some of their Burlington Plantation , in one of the first expansions of the campus. &#91; when? &#93; [7] ^ body:not( ):not( ) Mediratta, Avi; Bub, Sydney (October 5, 2016). "The Legacy of Slavery at Vanderbilt" . Vanderbilt Political Review . Archived from the original on June 17, 2018 . Retrieved June 16, 2018 . Although Cornelius Vanderbilt originally supported the Union, it was Frank Armstrong Crawford Vanderbilt, the Commodore''s wife and a Confederate sympathizer, who supposedly convinced him to donate money for the founding of Vanderbilt University. The university named Crawford House, on the Martha Rivers Ingram Commons, in her honor. ^ a b Fuselier, Kathryn; Yee, Robert (October 17, 2016). "The Legacy of Slavery at Vanderbilt: Our Forgotten Past" . Vanderbilt Historical Review . Archived from the original on October 2, 2017 . Retrieved September 19, 2017 . ^ Glenn, Justin (2015). The Washingtons: A Family History: Volume 1: Seven Generations of the Presidential Branch . El Dorado Hills, California: Savas Beatie. p. 1895. ISBN 978-1-61121-285-3 . OCLC 8', '["clm_wiki_vanderbilt-university_demographics"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'place_sections_v2', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
