VALUES
  ('cs_new-york-university_history', 'plc_new-york-university', 'overview', 'History',
   'Private university in New York City, New York This article is about the private institution founded in 1831. For other uses, see University of New York . "NYU" redirects here. For the district in Japan, see Nyū District, Fukui . For the Elfen Lied character, see List of Elfen Lied characters § Nyu . New York University Former name University of the City of New-York (1831–1896) Motto Perstare et praestare ( Latin ) Motto in English "To persevere and to excel" Type Private research university Established April 21, 1831 &#59;&#32;195 years ago ( April 21, 1831 ) [1] Founder Albert Gallatin Accreditation MSCHE Academic affiliations AAU AITU NAICU [2] space-grant Endowment $7.28 billion (2025) [3] Budget $18.8 billion (including Langone); $4.3 billion (excluding Langone) (2025) [4] President Linda G. Mills Provost Georgina Dopico Faculty 5,094 (fall 2023) [5] Administrative staff 2,242 [6] [7] Students 61,890 (fall 2023) [5] Undergraduates 29,760 (fall 2023) [5] Postgraduates 27,578 (fall 2023) [5] Location New York City , United States 40°43′48″N 73°59′42″W &#xfeff; / &#xfeff; 40.73000°N 73.99500°W &#xfeff; / 40.73000; -73.99500 Campus 230 acres (93 ha) (Manhattan campus) [8] Large city [9] Other campuses Brooklyn Englewood Cliffs Los Angeles Mineola Washington Abu Dhabi Accra Berlin Buenos Aires Florence Havana London Madrid Paris Prague Shanghai Sydney Tel Aviv Tulsa Newspaper Washington Square News Colors Violet and white [10] Nickname Violets Sporting affiliations NCAA Division III – UAA Mascot Bobcat Website nyu New York University ( NYU ) is a private research university in New York City , United States. Chartered in 1831 by the New York State Legislature , [11] NYU was founded in 1832 by Albert Gallatin [12] as a non-denominational all-male institution near City Hall based on a curriculum focused on a secular education . [13] [14] The university moved in 1833 and has maintained its main campus in Greenwich Village surrounding Washington Square Park . [15] Since then, the university has added an engineering school in Brooklyn ''s MetroTech Center and graduate schools throughout Manhattan . [16] NYU is one of the largest private universities in the United States by enrollment, with a total of 51,848 enrolled students in 2021. [17] It is one of the most applied-to schools in the country and admissions are considered selective. [18] [19] [20] NYU''s main campus in New York City is organized into undergraduate schools in the fields of arts and science , indivi', '["clm_wiki_new-york-university_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'place_sections_v2', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   20, 1, 1, unixepoch());
