VALUES
  ('cs_new-york-university_demographics', 'plc_new-york-university', 'overview', 'Demographics',
   'University logo The university logo, the upheld torch , is derived from the Statue of Liberty , signifying NYU''s service to New York City. [1] The torch is depicted on both the NYU seal and the more abstract NYU logo, designed in 1965 by renowned graphic designer Tom Geismar of the branding and design firm Chermayeff &amp; Geismar . [2] There are at least two versions of the possible origin of the university color, violet . Some believe that it may have been chosen because violets are said to have grown abundantly in Washington Square and around the buttresses of the Old University Building. Others argue that the color may have been adopted because the violet was the flower associated with Athens , the center of learning in ancient Greece . ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Logos, Lockups, and University Seal" . NYC . Archived from the original on May 13, 2023 . Retrieved May 13, 2023 . ^ "A Chat With The Designer Of NYU''s Torch Logo" . NYU Local . November 16, 2016. Archived from the original on September 19, 2023 . Retrieved May 13, 2023 .', '["clm_wiki_new-york-university_demographics"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'place_sections_v2', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
