VALUES
  ('cs_united-states-coast-guard-academy_geography', 'plc_united-states-coast-guard-academy', 'overview', 'Geography',
   'Admission Aerial view of Washington Parade field and campus Unlike the other service academies, admission to the USCGA does not require a congressional nomination. This is due to the fervent objections of Captain John A. Henriques, the first Superintendent of the Revenue Cutter School of Instruction (later the Revenue Cutter Academy). His objection stemmed from years of poor political appointments in the U.S. Revenue Cutter Service''s bureaucracy. However, under the Compacts of Free Association between the United States and the Republics of Palau , Micronesia and the Marshall Islands , the USCGA is obliged to at all times have at least one student enrolled who is nominated by the governments of each of those states. [1] [2] [3] Each year more than 2,000 students apply and appointments are offered until the number accepting appointments to the incoming class numbers reaches approximately 400; the average entering class size is 300 cadets. [4] Those who have received appointments as cadets report to the USCGA in late June or early July for " Swab Summer ", a basic military training program designed to prepare them for the rigors of their Fourth Class year. After four years of study and training, approximately 250 of those cadets will graduate. About 40 percent of cadets are women. ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Repulbic of Palau Compact of Free Association" (PDF) . US Department of the Interior . 1 October 1994 . Retrieved 1 March 2026 . ^ "Agreement between the UNITED STATES OF AMERICA and the MARSHALL ISLANDS" (PDF) . US State Department . 30 April 2003 . Retrieved 1 March 2026 . ^ "Agreement between the UNITED STATES OF AMERICA and MICRONESIA" (PDF) . US State Department . 14 May 2003 . Retrieved 1 March 2026 . ^ Admissions: Frequently Asked Questions – Statistics Archived 9 November 2017 at the Wayback Machine U.S. Coast Guard. Retrieved 8 November 2017.', '["clm_wiki_united-states-coast-guard-academy_geography"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'place_sections_v2', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   30, 1, 1, unixepoch());
