  ('cs_in-country_geography', 'ent_in', 'overview', 'Geography',
   'Modern India Main article: History of India (1947–present) Mahatma Gandhi after a visit to the Presidency Jail, Calcutta , April 1938 The Capitol Complex in Chandigarh , commissioned after India''s 1947 partition The appointment in 1848 of Lord Dalhousie as Governor General of the East India Company set the stage for changes essential to a modern state: the consolidation and demarcation of sovereignty, the surveillance of the population, and the education of citizens. Technological changes—among them, railways, canals, and the telegraph—were introduced not long after their introduction in Europe . [1] [2] [3] [4] Disaffection with the company also grew during this time, culminating in the Indian Rebellion of 1857 . Fed by diverse resentments and perceptions, including invasive British-style social reforms, harsh land taxes, and summary treatment of some wealthy landowners and princes, the rebellion rocked many regions of northern and central India and shook the foundations of Company rule. [5] [6] After the rebellion was suppressed in 1858, the East India Company was disbanded, and the British government began to directly administer India . Proclaiming a unitary state and a gradual but limited British-style parliamentary system, [7] the new rulers also protected princes and landed gentry as a feudal safeguard against future unrest. [8] In the decades following, public life gradually emerged across India, eventually leading to the founding of the Indian National Congress in 1885. [9] [10] [11] [12] The rush of technology and the commercialisation of agriculture during the second half of the 19th century was marked by economic setbacks, and many small farmers became dependent on the whims of faraway markets. [13] There was an increase in the number of large-scale famines , [14] and, despite the risks of infrastructure development borne by Indian taxpayers, little industrial employment was generated for Indians. [15] However, commercial cropping, especially in the newly', '["clm_wiki_in-country_geography"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'place_sections_v2', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   30, 1, 1, unixepoch());
