VALUES
  ('cs_il-country_geography', 'ent_il', 'overview', 'Geography',
   'History Main article: History of Israel Further information: History of Israel (1948–present) For a chronological guide, see Timeline of Israeli history . Prehistory Further information: Prehistory of the Levant The Ubeidiya prehistoric site in northern Israel shows the presence of archaic humans around 1.5 million years ago. [1] The second-oldest evidence of anatomically modern humans outside Africa is a 200,000-year-old fossil from Misliya Cave on Mount Carmel. [2] The Natufian culture ( c. 10,000 BCE) may be linked to the Proto-Afroasiatic language [3] [4] and is notable for adopting sedentism before the advent of agriculture and the Neolithic Revolution . [5] Bronze and Iron Ages Further information: Ancient Israel and Judah Tel Megiddo , the ruins of a Canaanite and later Israelite city Early references to " Canaan " and "Canaanites" appear in ancient Near Eastern and Egyptian texts ( c. 2000 BCE); these populations were structured as politically independent city-states . [6] [7] During the Late Bronze Age (1550–1200 BCE), large parts of Canaan formed vassal states of the New Kingdom of Egypt . [8] As a result of the Late Bronze Age collapse , Canaan fell into chaos, and Egyptian control over the region collapsed. [9] [10] Ancestors of the Israelites are thought to have included ancient Semitic-speaking peoples native to this area. [11] &#58;&#8202;78–79&#8202; Modern archaeological accounts suggest that the Israelites and their culture branched out of the Canaanite peoples through the settlement of the central highlands and the development of a distinct monolatristic —and later monotheistic —religion centered on Yahweh . [12] [13] They spoke an archaic form of Hebrew , known as Biblical Hebrew . [14] Around the same time, the Philistines settled on the southern coastal plain . [15] [16] The Yavne-Yam ostracon , a Paleo-Hebrew inscription documenting administration in Judah Most modern scholars agree that the Exodus narrative in the Torah and Old Testament did ', '["clm_wiki_il-country_geography"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'place_sections_v2', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   30, 1, 1, unixepoch());
